    "conclusion": "Ordered sequence extraction succeeded. Single global temporal filters are neutral, but a two-component representation combining the uniform mean with a training-subject-only learned early-to-late contrast produces a small, repeatable gain. The 2048-cap version is the strongest zero-label independent decoder at 0.8316 and improves significantly over the original 1024 mean hierarchy; its 0.8799 balanced score is promising but remains exploratory because subject-level uncertainty crosses zero. Keep 0.8752 as the conservative balanced benchmark while reporting the multi-filter model separately."
